--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Previously flagged and now removed
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

@mercuryworkshop/scramjet — REMOVED. No longer a dependency, and no longer
present in any build output.

  Earlier revisions of this file carried an "UNRESOLVED LICENSING" warning
  against this package, because it gave three contradictory signals and no
  reading of them granted redistribution rights:

    - the upstream repository (https://github.com/MercuryWorkshop/scramjet)
      contains no LICENSE file, and the GitHub API reports `license: null`
    - its npm package.json declares "license": "MIT"
    - the published tarball ships a 661-line GNU AFFERO GENERAL PUBLIC LICENSE,
      Version 3 (19 November 2007)

  No licence at all defaults to all rights reserved; a metadata field is not a
  grant; and AGPL-3.0 cannot be sublicensed under MIT. Since vite.config.ts
  copied its prebuilt bundles into every web build, that question rode along in
  each distributed artifact.

  It backed the web-only rewriting proxy behind the browser panel. That panel is
  now desktop-only — the Electron shell's <webview> needs no proxy — so the
  package, its runtime files and the server-side egress route it fed were all
  removed rather than shipped under an unresolved claim.

  @mercuryworkshop/bare-mux was removed at the same time. It was a genuine
  MIT-licensed package (it shipped real MIT text, Copyright 2024 Mercury
  Workshop Inc., merely omitting the metadata field) and was NOT removed on
  licensing grounds — only because nothing used it once the proxy was gone.

